{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>They shall encamp.</b> And because the Kohathites are the most honored of all the Levites, Kohath was stationed on the south, for it is more honored than the west and than the north, and there is none eastward more honored than it. And because Gershon was Levi's firstborn, he has great precedence over Merari, for he bears the holy things as against Merari's burden; therefore Gershon encamped on the west like the standard of Ephraim, and Merari on the north like the standard of Dan, who is the firstborn of the maidservant. Now the Kohathites were alongside the standard of Reuben; therefore Korah joined with Dathan and Abiram. And I shall yet explain it:"], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:09.715313371Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}